==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 6~20 seconds<sup>180f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 6~20 seconds<sup>180f~600f</sup>.
*5 [[Dagshund]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 30~54 seconds<sup>900f~1,620f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 14.67~25.33 seconds<sup>440f~760f</sup>.
*2 [[Mr. Mole]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
*1 [[Croakley]] spawns after 83.33 seconds<sup>2,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Most of the stage's difficulty stems from Mr. Mole and Croakley's LD attacks stunlocking your units to death while the presence of the tanky Dagshund makes them near impossible to hit. All of the threats on the level are timed, leaving you with little opportunity to prepare for an onslaught. Abusing Dagshund with Wave Attackers will be your best means of hitting these dangerous backliners, but be sure to reserve lots of meatshields so Dagshunds and Celeboodles won't be able to overwhelm you.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]]: Slime is able to deliver a burst of damage through a level 5 wave attack, something made readily possible due to Dagshund's long attack animation that can add up over time and eventually stop Mr. Mole or Croakley from doing too much damage. Slime's relatively high speed means as long as Croakley and Mr. Mole aren't getting close enough not much timing is needed to get a hit.
*[[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Hermit Cat]]: Hermit is able to rapidly fire level 3 wave attacks through a three-part multi-hit. His low range makes him vulnerable to Dagshund but also makes it easier to avoid being hit by Mr. Mole and Croakley. Hermit's True Form works even better, with level 5 wave attacks sniping threats from afar while the reduced cooldown and health boost dramatically increases his potential damage.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can outranges Dagshund, deals a lot of damage with its single-target attacks while being cheap for what it does, allowing it to accumulate damage like wave attackers. Eliminating Dagshunds before more arrive makes it much easier to keep your wave attackers alive, as most wave attackers can't kill Dagshund on their own and allowing them to stack unchecked can pose a huge risk to them. Even if Dagshund destroys Can Can, you can always send more and keep fighting.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Bahamut can be used in a similar fashion to Can Can, in that his huge DPS rips Dagshund and just about any threat to shreds if protected well. Mr. Mole can even reset his attack animation. Just make sure your meatshields can catch up and beware of Croakley's attack.

